{"abstract":[{"text":"Ready-made collapse resolvers.","type":"text"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swiduxpersistence\/entitycollapse"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"EntityCollapse"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"text":"Why the hook takes the whole collection","type":"heading","anchor":"Why-the-hook-takes-the-whole-collection"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A per-ID resolver would only handle half the problem. Rows sharing an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"id"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"are one failure mode; the other is a "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"singleton","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" — an entity an app holds"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"exactly one of, such as a settings record. Created independently on two"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"fresh installs, two singletons have "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"different","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" UUIDs, so nothing groups"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"them and no ID-keyed resolver can ever see the conflict. A"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"([E]) -> [E]"},{"type":"text","text":" hook covers both, plus general garbage collection, with one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"API."}]},{"level":2,"text":"The determinism requirement","type":"heading","anchor":"The-determinism-requirement"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A resolver must be a pure function of "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"replicated content","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" — never"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"persistentModelID"},{"type":"text","text":", never a local timestamp, never array position. Every"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"device must compute the same survivor set from the same rows. A resolver"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that doesn’t reintroduces the mutual-tombstone loss the write path is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"designed to avoid: two devices pick different survivors, each tombstones the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"other’s, and after sync "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"both","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" rows are gone."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"It must also be idempotent — "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"collapse(collapse(rows))"},{"type":"text","text":" must keep the same"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"IDs as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"collapse(rows)"},{"type":"text","text":". This is checked with an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"assert"},{"type":"text","text":" in debug builds."}]},{"level":2,"text":"Collapse removes IDs, not rows","type":"heading","anchor":"Collapse-removes-IDs-not-rows"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A resolver’s output is read as "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"the set of IDs that should exist and what","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"each should contain","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":". An ID the resolver drops is deleted, including every"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"row carrying it. Several rows that share a "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"surviving","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" ID are all updated"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to the survivor’s value, and none of them is deleted."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"That asymmetry is deliberate, and it is the whole reason the singleton case"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is the one this hook really solves. Deleting an ID is safe because "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"id"},{"type":"text","text":" is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"replicated: every device independently computes the same set of doomed IDs"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and issues the same deletions. Deleting one of several rows that share an ID"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"not","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" safe — nothing replicated distinguishes them, so two devices can"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"pick different physical rows to keep, each tombstones the other’s, and both"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"are lost."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Rows sharing an ID need no deletion anyway: writes already converge across"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"every matching row and reads already collapse to one value per ID (see"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/EntityDB"},{"type":"text","text":"), so duplicates cost storage and nothing else."}]}]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/EntityCollapse","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"topicSections":[{"title":"Type Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/EntityCollapse\/byID(preferring:)"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Type-Methods"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence"]]},"kind":"symbol","sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"SwiduxPersistence"}],"externalID":"s:17SwiduxPersistence14EntityCollapseO","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"EntityCollapse"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"EntityCollapse","kind":"identifier"}],"roleHeading":"Enumeration","symbolKind":"enum","role":"symbol","title":"EntityCollapse"},"references":{"doc://SwiduxPersistence/documentation/SwiduxPersistence/EntityCollapse":{"url":"\/documentation\/swiduxpersistence\/entitycollapse","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/EntityCollapse","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"EntityCollapse","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"EntityCollapse","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"EntityCollapse","type":"topic","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Ready-made collapse resolvers.","type":"text"}]},"doc://SwiduxPersistence/documentation/SwiduxPersistence/EntityDB":{"url":"\/documentation\/swiduxpersistence\/entitydb","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/EntityDB","fragments":[{"text":"actor","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"EntityDB","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"EntityDB","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"EntityDB","type":"topic","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A generic "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@ModelActor"},{"type":"text","text":" that reads and writes any "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/PersistableModel"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},"doc://SwiduxPersistence/documentation/SwiduxPersistence/PersistableModel":{"url":"\/documentation\/swiduxpersistence\/persistablemodel","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/PersistableModel","fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"PersistableModel","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"PersistableModel","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"PersistableModel","type":"topic","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The generated SwiftData "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Model"},{"type":"text","text":" shadow for a "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/PersistableEntity"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},"doc://SwiduxPersistence/documentation/SwiduxPersistence/EntityCollapse/byID(preferring:)":{"url":"\/documentation\/swiduxpersistence\/entitycollapse\/byid(preferring:)","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Collapses rows sharing an ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"id"},{"text":" down to one, keeping the winner of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"choose"},{"type":"text","text":". Rows with unique IDs pass through untouched."}],"title":"byID(preferring:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/EntityCollapse\/byID(preferring:)","fragments":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"byID","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"E","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"text":"preferring","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": (","kind":"text"},{"text":"E","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"E","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"E","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ([","kind":"text"},{"text":"E","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"]) -> [","kind":"text"},{"text":"E","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"]","kind":"text"}]},"doc://SwiduxPersistence/documentation/SwiduxPersistence":{"title":"SwiduxPersistence","type":"topic","role":"collection","kind":"symbol","abstract":[],"url":"\/documentation\/swiduxpersistence","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence"}}}